# Higher-order methods

*Take a function, return a function, or both.*

## Take a function — inject behaviour

```java
static <T> List<T> filter(List<T> in, Predicate<T> keep) {
    var out = new ArrayList<T>();
    for (T x : in) if (keep.test(x)) out.add(x);
    return out;
}
```

The method owns the loop; the caller owns the criterion → the **Strategy pattern**, as a lambda. Also: `retry(3, () -> httpGet(url))`.

## Return a function — configure

```java
static Function<Integer,Integer> adder(int by) { return n -> n + by; }
var add10 = adder(10);   // captures `by` — currying / partial application
```

## Both — decorate

```java
static <T,R> Function<T,R> logged(Function<T,R> f) {
    return t -> { R r = f.apply(t); log(t, r); return r; };
}
```

Memoize, time, cache — wrap **without touching** the original. → the `Stream` API (module 07).
